 ## Overview
-The Compact Pointer Tree is a tree-based data structure and traversal algorithm designed for the interactive visualization of terabyte-scale RGBA volumetric data with voxel-level details [S1][S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of rendering massive, sparse volumes on GPUs by combining wavelet-based color compression with compact 8-bit relative pointers [S1][S2, unofficial]. Unlike standard octrees that use fixed 8 children, this structure uses a variable branching factor $N$ ($2 \le N \le 6$) to optimize memory usage, enabling real-time frame rates for 8K resolution volumes [S1][S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Tree-based structures (Octree, Pointer Tree, Sparse Voxel DAG)](4139-tree-based-structures-octree-pointer-tree-sparse-voxel-dag.md) by introducing recursive color attribute compression and hierarchical DDA traversal that avoids full root traversal for subsequent accesses [S1][S2, unofficial].
+The Compact Pointer Tree is a tree-based data structure and traversal algorithm designed for the interactive visualization of terabyte-scale RGBA volumetric data with voxel-level details [S1][S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of rendering massive, sparse volumes on GPUs by combining wavelet-based color compression with compact 8-bit relative pointers [S1][S2, unofficial]. Unlike standard octrees that use a fixed branching factor of 8, this structure uses a variable branching factor $N$ ($2 \le N \le 6$) to optimize memory usage, enabling real-time frame rates for 8K resolution volumes [S1][S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Tree-based structures (Octree, Pointer Tree, Sparse Voxel DAG)](4139-tree-based-structures-octree-pointer-tree-sparse-voxel-dag.md) by introducing recursive color attribute compression and hierarchical DDA traversal that avoids full root traversal for subsequent accesses [S1][S2, unofficial].
 
